# Session scratch: mutation-probe harnesses and per-step gate logs. Kept in-tree
# rather than in $TMPDIR because the OS evicts temp files mid-session and
# `pnpm test:coverage` deletes `coverage/` — both have cost the only copy of a
# failing run. Untracked and unlinted on purpose; never a commit input.
.gate-logs/

# WorkBuddy project data: session notes live here and are written by an agent,
# not by a human editing the repository. It reached a public commit once — via a
# `git add -A` inside PR #476, which is exactly how it would happen again — and
# notes are not part of what this package publishes (`files` is a whitelist and
# never listed it). Untracked on purpose: the directory is still read and
# written locally, it just is not a commit input.
.workbuddy/
